{
  "collections": [
    {
      "description": "Chess rule-conformance battery for the eval-chess-backend FastAPI service (POST/GET /games, /games/{id}/moves, /legal-moves, /health, /metrics). Covers: legal & illegal moves (board left unchanged, move_history empty on rejection); kingside & queenside castling; castling-rights respected (kingside disallowed when the K right is absent in the FEN); cannot castle through an attacked square; en passant offered when the FEN's ep square is set and not when it is cleared, and the capture applies; promotion incl. underpromotion; a pinned piece cannot move; a move leaving one's own king in check is rejected; checkmate -> white_won; stalemate -> draw; the 50-move rule (start at halfmove clock 99) -> draw; threefold repetition (knight shuffle) -> draw; 404 for an unknown game; 422 for an unparseable move and for a bad FEN. All FENs and legal-move lists are python-chess-derived; draw assertions assume claim-aware game-over detection (board.is_game_over(claim_draw=True)).",
      "items": [
        "chess-01-health",
        "chess-02-metrics",
        "chess-03-create-legal",
        "chess-04-legal-move-e2e4",
        "chess-05-get-game-after-e4",
        "chess-06-create-illegal",
        "chess-07-illegal-move-rejected",
        "chess-08-unparseable-move-422",
        "chess-09-unknown-game-move-404",
